// A term generated by Easy-Sched's benchmark harness (generator.py, size "small",
// seed 3), run through the backend's rule compiler. Each candidate lists the
// normalised scoring features (0..1) the backend computed; a slot's score is the
// weighted sum, exactly as in the app. Only eligible pairs appear: eligibility is
// decided before scoring. People's names and course titles are made up for
// readability; the generator emits "Student 7" and "Synthetic Course 2".
// Backend result with default weights: 18 of 22 slots, total fit 127.88.

export type Feature = "grade" | "experience" | "recommendation" | "preference" | "skill" | "utaBonus";

